WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:08.900
The stakes are very high for newly-elected South Korean president Moon Jae-in.

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:12.200
He faces the dangers of Kim Jong-un of North Korea,

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:15.480
who has increased the pace of his missile and nuclear tests,

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:17.900
and is seeking to show us in the United States

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:21.820
that he could put a nuclear warhead on a missile capable of hitting our homeland.

00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:24.440
That's not just a threat to us;

00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:28.140
it's a threat to the entirety of the alliance system in Northeast Asia.

00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:33.220
We've been working closely with our allies in Japan and South Korea on increased defense cooperation.

00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:38.900
We need strong allies working together, but Japan and Korea have had difficulties in the past.

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:41.480
However, given the sobering nature of the threat,

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:46.540
Moon has indicated he will continue with this defense cooperation, even if cautiously.

00:00:46.540 --> 00:00:49.980
He is walking into a new policy by the Trump administration

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:55.060
that's seeking to put maximum pressure on North Korea -  and on China -  to isolate the Hermit Kingdom.

00:00:55.060 --> 00:00:59.520
We cannot succeed, though, if the Korean president puts brakes on this campaign.

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:02.340
Given the sobering nature of Kim's danger,

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:06.100
I think Moon will continue with the tougher policies of his predecessor.

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:11.420
